  <!--
    The M1A2's AGT1500 gas turbine and Allison X1100-3B cross-drive.
    - 1,500 shp (1,118 kW) at 3,000 rpm output speed; turbine inlet about 1,193 degrees C (secondary: an AlliedSignal data sheet
      archived by Chalmers University, 1997). Its fuel use at idle is high (the earlier archetype's 0.6 idle share, authored: no
      absolute idle figure was found; Honeywell's digital control gives 20% less at idle).
    - Gearbox: Allison X1100-3B, four forward and two reverse, for engines up to 1,500 hp and vehicles up to 75 tons (primary:
      Allison); ratios authored. Mass 63,080 kg, the M1A2's 69.54 short tons (secondary: FAS). Top speed 42 mph (67.6 km/h),
      governed (secondary: FAS); final drive 5.52 from it (our inference). Sprocket radius 0.33 m (authored).
